@ClearlyClaire @oneiros also, on "public clients", I'm not sure if it actually makes long-term sense to continue support for `POST /api/v1/apps` once we have implemented [OAuth Client ID Metadata Documents](https://drafts.aaronpk.com/draft-parecki-oauth-client-id-metadata-document/draft-parecki-oauth-client-id-metadata-document.html), since these are superior to DCR for federated many clients to many servers setups.

(Note: Client ID Metadata Documents are currently an I-D and have been put in front of the IETF OAuth working group at IETF 120 this week, where overall they were well received.

There's also further considerations around public clients vs confidential, which requires things like prohibiting certain grant flows for certain clients. There's also the question of whether `jwks_uri` is supported, which enables confidential clients potentially (I still need to fully understand this part of the OAuth specs)
